Z||000006||bHooper||01-24-2001||09:30 AM||||the net is a wonderfull tool to meet people!  i have met a few people from the forum, and when i was single, i too used it to meet, and date.<P>the only draw back that i found to using it in that manner, was the old "they aren't always what the make themselves out to be" thing.  people could have the best personality, online, and be total duds in person.  and yes, believe it or not, they do even physically misrepresent themselves, from time to time!  got caught on that one ::shudder to think about::<P>but you know what, it is probably as much fun as any other method of meeting people, and it does allow you to stretch around the globe and talk to people you probably would never have met otherwise.<P>Rae, i think it would be an excellent idea.  but as an alternative, you may want to set up a time on the chat option for people to get together.  that could be a good start.<P>Jean Marie, as for Lisa being the most popular... i think it is probably better said that she is the most visable.  by that, i mean, she has a web site with photo's, people can recognize her, she goes to car show's and she lives in 2 areas that have quite a few forum members.  therefore, people seem to know her a little more.<P>from my discussions with you, you are ever bit as nice of a person as Lisa.  use the forum, the shows and the comunity, and you can meet a lot of people!  (btw, how are the shocks/struts?)<P>really the only true way to overcome loneliness, is to increase your exposure to other people, be open and friendly, and have confidence (but not too much).  i am no expert in relationships, but i have done enough things wrong to know what not to do  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(i hope i didnt sound condescending, or better than, or anything, i just wanted to offer a bit of my own experiience and observations to this)<P>hoop||||reg||1
