Z||000016||bHooper||01-24-2001||04:44 PM||||now... now... i didn't say that i was better than anyone.  but compliments are always welcome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  jk<P>i didnt intend to open up a can of worms, just mearly to pass on my own personal experience over the past several years.  i'm sorry if anyone took my conversing as otherwise!<P>i have had plenty of ups and downs with relationships.  in fact, now that i think of it, had it not been for the internet, i probably would not be getting married this summer!  even though, i have known my fiance' for 4 years, we really didn't start comunicating and getting to know each other until she moved away.  weused the net to communicate, and joke back and forth! eventually it led to something more.<P>Jean, as for Lisa (and please correct me if i'm wrong, Lisa), I think Jonathon (Slammed Fiero) is her boyfriend.  So how they talk to each other, doesn't matter, does it?  I see Lisa, and you just like everyone else here on the forum... a car nut!  Why else would we be here to begin with?  I've met Lisa, might even help her put her springs in her car, when she come's to town.  My girlfriend has met Lisa also, they might ride horse's together some, this summer.  We all share a common interest that allows us to learn and develope friendships with each other!<P>As I've said, or tried to say, the net is a wonderfull place to meet all kinds of people, and make new friends.  Either people you can go to the movies with, rebuild a distributor with, or chat with over thousands of miles!  I list you in that.  I enjoyed our conversations, last month.  But I can probably also list about 25 other people, that I have met on the net that I still chat with, or do things with.<P>sorry, i hope i haven't stuck my damnd foot in my mouth.  i just wanted to impart a thought, or common feeling.  maybe i should stay out of the off topic sesion... unless its to piss off the nascar folk with talk of F1 superiority!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||01-24-2001||04:47 PM||||I have to agree with JMW , I really don't like the way a lot of guys treat her , there are a few on the forum that are pretty bad , no one here. But rest assured Lisa is very good at voicing her oppinion and doesn't take SH** from anyone , not me , not anyone. She can yell damm loud and hits pretty damm hard when she wants too...<P>No i didn't say much of anything to her at the fiero show , we sat together at the banquet and talked but that was aboot it....<P>I also find a lot of guys don't like me for being with her. there are some damm immature people in this world. One guy was saying how much faster his car is gonna be than mine when it's done and telling Lisa all this... SHe doesn't CARE!!<P>thank you for listening , i will get off the soapbox now now. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
