Z||000019||FieroLisa||01-24-2001||05:45 PM||||Ok I just have to add more here.<P>jmw- well i'm not going to insult you in any way, so don't take anything I say to be that way, I'm sure you're extremely nice and probably very knowledgable about cars, just like every other female  fiero-obsessed owner I've met. But in a previous reply on this post you said something like "but FieroLisa gets all the attention" and now you say you don't want the attention I get.  As for the "attention" I get, people on this forum are not trying to get a date with me or sleep with me, they are just being nice guys. emphasis on being "guys". Especially being at school and dealing with 18 to 20-some year old guys, I'm just used to it. I like to joke around with them, just like they joke around with me, I know they are kidding. I feel like I've got a lot of friends here, even if I don't really know most of you!<P>roger- thanks for the compliments, but you should be getting them, not me- you let me use your garage, tools, AND drive your kick @ss car! So thanks!<P>And to shut up now, I hope to see/meet many of you at Daytona, Carlisle, and the other shows I go to this year with my new GT!<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||DaRkLoRD||01-24-2001||05:57 PM||||I personally don't want to meet a girl over the internet.. I use ICQ to talk to people from back home, and I've made many friends from all over the world.. some of my closest friends live in New Zealand. they're like penpals I talk to in real-time.. but as for girls, I prefer to meet them in real life.. which is probably why I'm single.. lol..<BR>(I don't get out much.. I don't drink so I don't go to bars/clubs etc)<P>Regarding FieroLisa, I don't think I've spoken to her other than a brief welcome message. A few of my friends are "players", and I feel it makes other guys look bad by being lumped together with guys that treat girls badly, such as when some women say "all guys are pigs".. My biggest fault in this issue is I often refer to young women as "chicks"... then again, compared to one guy who calls his girlfriend "his b*tch", I guess I'm not so bad... (at least I'm using it as an affectionate term)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000021||jmw||01-24-2001||06:10 PM||||Well, obviously FieroLisa doesn't need ME defending her! [BTW, I was mainly referring to your AGE, darlin']. If you enjoy all the innuendo and can take care of yourself, that's great! Have at it! All I'm saying is be careful. In my experience, sometimes the guys you think are harmless turn out to be the most dangerous. If you have friends looking out for you, you're lucky.<P>Also (and this is the last I'll say on the subject) I really DON'T want attention from guys just because of my looks. And that AIN'T 'cause I'm ugly. I just want someone who's into more than "entertainment".||||reg||12
Z||000022||RaeQwan||01-25-2001||05:19 AM||||ya know I once had a girl tell me, Oh My God Dont Touch Me.. coulda been cuz I had my snake wrapped around my neck.. something bout a 4foot python ppl dont like.. chicks must dig my car and my snakes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> otherwise.. they be out that door.. or if they get rowdy enough.. out that bloody window..<P>------------------<BR>Ray - AIM: WookieeNC<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Fiero Coupe</A> - <A HREF="http://www.CarolinaFieros.com" TARGET=_blank>Carolina Fieros</A> - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.net" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Network</A>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Motorhead||01-26-2001||06:49 PM||||As a 46 year old male who has had his share of relationships I have one comment to make from experience.<BR>"Treat others as you would like to be treated"!  Gender not withstanding!<BR>In my "younger" days I was guilty of treating the fairer sex as less than fair.<BR>The attitude that seems to pollute the male ego at younger ages consists of a an innate desire to be cool to women.<BR>  I take back the younger ages comment.  The attitude sometimes lasts much longer!<BR>  This is pure BS which fogs the thinking process.  I believe it's referred to as "thinking with the wrong head"!<BR>As an individual guilty of commiting that sin more than once, I know from where I speak!<BR>Sorry so long! Here is the end of the story.<BR>I have known my third wife for twenty years now, and only recently have I figured out that a family is not an easy thing to maintain.  <BR>My 13 year old son son is my greatest accomplishment in this life, and my marriage has been my toughest endeavor.  But both are the greatest thing any man can hope to attain.  <BR>The biggest regret I have is that I wasn't bright enough to figure all this stuff out sooner.  Like maybe 25 years ago.<BR>But that's OK!  My kid is an honors student who excells in every sport he attempts.<BR>My wife is just like the rest of us mortals.  Strong as hell sometimes, and driven to tears at others.  And I'm just some poor male schmuck who "just figured it out"!<BR>Sorry for the long post.  Just had to say it!<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike     <BR>Oh yea!  She also loves the Fieros!  Makes life just a little more pleasant!<BR>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"<BR>  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1372350&a=10234998&p=38686771&Sequence=0">  <p>[This message has been edited by Motorhead (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||1
